-- title:
--   dim W[[u,v]]/(uv-π)=2 over a discrete valuation ring
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring that is Noetherian, local and an integral domain, and let $\pi \in W$ be an element such that the maximal ideal of $W$ equals the principal ideal $(\pi)$ and $\pi \neq 0$; thus $W$ is a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $\pi$. Write $R_\pi$ for `UVCrossingModel W π`, the quotient of the two-variable formal power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$, i.e. $W[[X_0,X_1]]$, by the ideal generated by the single element $X_0 X_1 - \pi$ (with $\pi$ entering through the constant-coefficient map). The assertion is that the Krull dimension of $R_\pi$, taken as the supremum of lengths of chains of prime ideals in the value type $\mathbb{N}_\infty$ with a bottom element, equals $2$.
--
--   This is the dimension half of the classical statement that $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$ is a regular two-dimensional local ring, the local model at a supersingular point of the modular curve with $\Gamma_0(p)$-structure in the Deligne–Rapoport/Katz–Mazur description. It feeds the further analysis of this local model, in particular the structural results on its height-one primes and on elements expressed as a unit times a power of $U$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_ringKrullDim_eq_two.lean

